course: dictionary
lesson: 13553
title: Formal words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are big and formal. You will meet them in the news, in official letters and in old books. Impropriety is one of them, but you can work it out from its parts. «Im-» often means not, and «proper» means right or correct. So impropriety is behaviour that is not right.
explain: «The manager was accused of financial impropriety when money went missing from the club.» The clues are money going missing and accused. The manager did not handle the money honestly. Always ask: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: In old stories, impropriety can mean a small rude act. «The boy's impropriety at dinner was talking with his mouth full.» Here it means bad manners, not a crime. The same word can be strong or small, so look at the clues each time.
fact: Impropriety means behaviour that is not right, honest or acceptable.
fact: «Financial impropriety» means handling money in a dishonest way.
fact: «Impropriety» can also mean a small, rude act that breaks the rules of good behaviour.
fact: You will mostly meet this word in news reports and formal speech.
fact: Phrases to know: «no impropriety», «accused of impropriety» and «the appearance of impropriety».
exercise: «The mayor was accused of financial impropriety.» What does this mean? | Keeping a pet | Winning a race | *Handling money in a dishonest way | Giving away free cakes
exercise: «The old lady was shocked by the young man's impropriety at the table.» What is the impropriety? | A long, quiet walk | Playing a game | Lovely, kind words | *A rude act that broke the rules of good manners
exercise: «The club said there was no impropriety in the sale of the tickets.» What does no impropriety mean? | A big sale happened | Everyone was late | *Nothing wrong or dishonest happened | The tickets were free for all
test: Which phrase shows someone was blamed for wrong behaviour? | *accused of impropriety | on the bus | the sunny morning | a bag of apples
test: Impropriety is best described as: | a type of weather | a long journey | *behaviour that is not right or acceptable | a kind, helpful act
exam: Jayden says impropriety means a kind deed. What is the correct meaning? | A long, quiet walk | A kind deed to help others | *Behaviour that is not right or acceptable | A happy, joyful party
